<title>GERMANY: German air cargo up 9.7pct in November 1996.</title>
<headline>German air cargo up 9.7pct in November 1996.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total air cargo flown to and from Germany increased 9.7 percent in November to 185,353 tonnes, the monthly traffic report of the German airports association ADV said.</p>
<p>The following table shows total, flown and trucked air cargo volumes in tonnes at international German airports in November 1996.</p>
<p> AIRPORT	    FLOWN    TRUCKED  TOTAL    PCT CHANGE</p>
<p> Berlin (total)    3,460     549     4,009   up   21.3</p>
<p> - Tegel	     1,798     505     2,303   up   11.2</p>
<p> - Tempelhof	    20	 0	  20   down 25.9</p>
<p> - Schoenefeld     1,642	44     1,686   up   39.7</p>
<p> Bremen		  251   2,167     2,418   up   19.3</p>
<p> Dresden		 137     201	 338   down 23.0</p>
<p> Duesseldorf	 5,791     n/a	 n/a	   n/a</p>
<p> Frankfurt	 125,060     n/a	 n/a	   n/a</p>
<p> Hamburg	     3,172     n/a	 n/a	   n/a</p>
<p> Hannover	    1,357     n/a	 n/a	   n/a</p>
<p> Cologne	    31,026   3,587    34,613   up   19.6</p>
<p> Leipzig/Halle	 304     106	 410   up    7.6</p>
<p> Munich		8,731     n/a	 n/a	   n/a</p>
<p> Muenster		 88   1,176     1,264   up   10.3</p>
<p> Nuremberg	   4,132   2,567     6,699   up    3.7</p>
<p> Saarbruecken	   14     141	 155   up   98.7</p>
<p> Stuttgart	   1,830   5,504     7,334   up   26.8</p>
<p>    TOTAL	  185,353     n/a	 n/a	   n/a</p>
<p>*Notes: No overall air cargo total is given as several large airports with known large trucking volumes including Frankfurt, Munich and Duesseldorf do not release trucking figures. - Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
